    "body": "## Purpose\n\nFix two shutdown races in the filesystem KV-offload thread pool:\n\n- `shutdown()` resets `_inflight_jobs` to zero when cancelling queued tasks. An already-running job can then finish and decrement it to -1, causing a subsequent `wait_idle()` to block indefinitely even after every worker has exited.\n- After `shutdown(wait=False)`, `wait_idle()` can observe the cleared count and return while a worker is still copying data.\n\nDo not decrement the cleared count after shutdown. When shutdown has started, join workers outside the condition lock before returning from `wait_idle()`. Queued tasks remain cancelled, including the queued portion of a partially executed job.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nAn event-controlled regression in the existing filesystem-tier suite covers waiting before/after the active task completes, with/without a cancelled task in the same job.\n\n```bash\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/v1/kv_offload/tiering/test_fs_tier.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_offload/tiering/test_tiering_offloading.py -q\n\n.venv/bin/python -m pre_commit run --hook-stage manual --files \\\n  vllm/v1/kv_offload/tiering/fs/thread_pool.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_offload/tiering/test_fs_tier.py\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n- Regression on unmodified production code: **3 failed, 1 passed** (one hang and two premature returns).\n- Fixed filesystem-tier and tiering-manager suites: **104 passed**.\n- All applicable manual pre-commit hooks passed, including mypy for Python 3.10–3.13.\n- Filesystem tests exercise real disk I/O with both Python and native paths. The native filesystem extension was rebuilt from the tested base, `6ebb5bd64f5ef75dbe1471ee88c009003b3d03ec`. No model-generation benchmark was run.\n\n## Duplicate-work check\n\nSearched open PRs for `DualQueueThreadPool`, `wait_idle shutdown`, and `offload shutdown`. No matching fix was found. #44541 introduced cache-reset draining; this addresses the pool's shutdown accounting and active-I/O wait. #57506 concerns CPU transfer-buffer ownership, not this filesystem thread pool.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, regression tests, and local validation.\n",
